## R6 canonical semantics

`item.transfer` remains the public command. P1 M4 interprets an occupied target as follows:

- same definition -> existing canonical stack transfer;
- incompatible definition + whole carried stack -> one atomic canonical slot-location swap;
- incompatible definition + partial carried quantity -> `SWAP_REQUIRES_FULL_STACK`;
- stale target item/slot mismatch -> `SWAP_TARGET_MISMATCH` without the requested swap;
- hotbar occupied-slot swap is intentionally not reinterpreted in R6 (`SWAP_HOTBAR_UNSUPPORTED`).

For cross inventory/container swaps the compatibility membership arrays are updated, while `location.slot_index` remains authoritative slot identity. No local UI mutation becomes Item Graph truth.

